  "tldr": "On one joint infinite-volume law carrying iid innovations, the generated graph and outcomes, and Bernoulli assignments, the exposure-IPW error splits exactly into a conditionally centered assignment coordinate and a Palm-population coordinate. The project derives their joint independent Gaussian limit, identifies \\(\\Omega_{\\mathrm{ann}}=\\Omega_{\\mathrm{des}}+\\Omega_{\\mathrm{pop}}\\), and asks the load-bearing random-metric question needed to prove that Leung's unchanged sample-mean-centered graph HAC estimates this full variance, with \\(R_n\\to\\Omega_{\\mathrm{pop}}\\). The local-chord law has an explicit admissible constant tuple, positive population variance, and shared graph--outcome innovations that violate the network-exogeneity premise of \\cite{Leung2019b}. An explicit stationary nonergodic triangular sequence lies outside the headline class and shows that the estimator in Theorem 4 of \\cite{Leung2022ANI} converges to the assignment variance one while the normalized estimator has variance two because sample centering removes the invariant shock; homogeneous effects recover the fixed-population result, and uniform Wald coverage supports a population-inference reanalysis of \\cite{BondEtAl2012} subject to data access and model diagnostics.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "Theorem 4 and Remark 2 of \\cite{Leung2022ANI} interpret the sample-centered graph-HAC remainder as finite-population heterogeneity and leave its superpopulation limit model-dependent; on a stationary nonergodic triangular sequence, that same named estimator can erase an order-one invariant component. Theorem 4.2 on pp. 27--28 of \\cite{Leung2019b} proves path-distance HAC validity under network exogeneity, and Remark 4.3 on p. 29 identifies why that premise matters; it does not cover graph and outcome heterogeneity generated by common innovations. Proposition 4.1 of \\cite{KojevnikovMarmerSong2021} begins with conditional centering and likewise does not treat a quadratic selected by an endogenous shortest-path event.",
    "niche": "A stationary ergodic local-innovation law can turn Leung's fixed-population remainder into repeated-network population fluctuation while allowing the graph metric and conditional means to share innovations, but only if the observed metric captures the Palm covariance without a persistent distance-selection term. The ergodicity boundary must exclude invariant row shocks that sample centering removes.",
